# Guiding Center 4d (Tokamak): 1st Poincaré Integral Invariant with Gauss-Legendre VPRK Methods and Projections

The first Poincaré integral invariant

```math
I_{1} = \oint_{\gamma} \vartheta_{i} (q) \, dq^{i}
```

of the four-dimensional guiding centre dynamics, on the same loop as the
[Gauss-Legendre Runge-Kutta page](guiding-center-4d-poincare-1st-tokamak-firk-gauss.md): a circle of
radius ``0.1`` in the poloidal plane of the medium-size axisymmetric tokamak about ``(R, Z) = (1.75,
0)``, at ``u = 0.5`` and ``\mu = 10^{-3}``.

Here the dynamics is integrated in its variational formulation, with the Gauss-Legendre variational
partitioned Runge-Kutta methods and each of the projections onto the constraint submanifold —
comparing the methods that preserve the structure of the dynamics with those that do not is the
point of these pages. The internal stage projection has no integrator in
GeometricIntegrators 0.16 and its runs fail here, as they do on the trajectory pages.

Each method is run over the same time interval at four time steps, ``\Delta t \in \{10, 5, 2, 1\}``,
whose relative errors are drawn as four curves in one figure, as on the
[Gauss-Legendre Runge-Kutta page](guiding-center-4d-poincare-1st-tokamak-firk-gauss.md). The
projection is what separates the runs: over this interval the unprojected method loses 3·10⁻¹ of the
invariant at ``\Delta t = 10`` and 3·10⁻³ at ``\Delta t = 1``, its symmetric projection 3·10⁻⁵ and
5·10⁻¹¹.

```julia
run_poincare(:tokamak, iodeproblem, "Guiding Center 4d Tokamak", tableaus_vprk_gauss())
```
